        "source_symbol": "prior_location_scale_threshold",
        "description": "Return prior-only rolling mean plus multiplier times standard deviation. At index i use values[max(0, i-history):i], excluding the current value. Return None until at least minimum prior observations exist. Empty input returns an empty list. Require 1 <= minimum <= history and 0 <= ddof < minimum; all counts are Python integers. Values and multiplier are finite Python real numbers, excluding booleans. Multiplier may be zero or negative. NumPy float64 reductions define arithmetic; reject conversion or reduction overflow. Preserve input. Missing-value handling, comparisons, labels and application-specific multiplier choices belong to the caller.",
